@startuml
title UC6 - Explore Story - Test Cases

map "TC-UC6-01: Progress through story chapter" as TC1 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC6-01
  Test Case Name => Successfully progress through a story chapter
  Description => Verify player can read story content, make choices, and advance to next chapter
  Preconditions => 1. Player is logged in \n 2. Player has a starter Pokemon \n 3. Story data loaded from story.json
  Test Case Input => Current chapter: Chapter 1 \n Player choice: Option A (explore forest)
  Expected Output => 1. Story text displayed correctly \n 2. Player choice processed \n 3. Next event triggered (wild encounter or NPC) \n 4. Progress auto-saved at chapter transition
  Steps => 1. Select Continue Story from Main Menu \n 2. System loads Chapter 1 \n 3. Read story text \n 4. Select Option A \n 5. System processes choice \n 6. Verify next event triggers \n 7. Complete event \n 8. Verify progress auto-saved
  Default Value Preserving => Player story progress updated in GameSession
}

map "TC-UC6-02: Exit story and return to menu" as TC2 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC6-02
  Test Case Name => Exit story exploration without losing progress
  Description => Verify player can exit story and return to Main Menu with progress intact
  Preconditions => 1. Player is in story exploration \n 2. Player has made progress in current chapter
  Test Case Input => Action: Exit story during Chapter 3
  Expected Output => 1. Player returns to Main Menu \n 2. Progress preserved \n 3. Re-entering story resumes at Chapter 3
  Steps => 1. During story chapter 3, select Exit \n 2. Verify return to Main Menu \n 3. Select Continue Story again \n 4. Verify story resumes at Chapter 3 \n 5. Verify all progress intact
  Default Value Preserving => Story progress maintained at last checkpoint
}

@enduml
